.SH "Typedef Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "typedef uint64_t \fBschultz_handle\fP"

.PP
Opaque object identity\&. A handle packs a table index in the low 32 bits and a generation counter in the high 32 bits\&. Because the generation of a live slot is never zero, a valid handle is never zero, and a handle naming a destroyed object fails its generation check instead of being dereferenced\&.
.PP
Hosts see a plain 64 bit integer\&. Pointers never cross the boundary\&. 
.PP
